Task complete and committed as 7e046fc. ✓

What I did (all in `src/setup.rs` + one doc line):

1. Tests first — 8 new tests covering:
   • Overwrite creates <path>.bak with the original contents
   • Unmanaged key (auto_watch = true) survives into the new file
   • Managed keys not duplicated — new value wins, exactly one model = line, old base_url dropped too
   • Fresh save: no .bak, no preserved comment (existing behavior untouched)
   • Paired negative (Day 122 lesson): old file with only managed keys → nothing appended
   • Section boundary: [permissions] keys don't get mis-appended as top-level
   • Unit test for preserved_unmanaged_lines skipping comments/blanks
   • User-config path (config.toml.bak via XDG override, #[serial])

2. Implementation — extracted the shared logic into write_config_with_backup:
   • MANAGED_CONFIG_KEYS = ["provider", "model", "base_url"] (matches `generate_config_contents` exactly)
   • preserved_unmanaged_lines does the simple line-based top-level scan, stopping at the first [ line
   • backup_path appends .bak (avoiding with_extension, which would have replaced .toml)
   • Both save_config_to_file and save_config_to_user_file route through it — public signatures unchanged

3. Wizard feedback — the interactive wizard checks existence before saving and prints "Previous config backed up to <path>.bak (unmanaged settings preserved)" when it overwrote something.

4. Docs — quick-start.md's wizard note now mentions the backup + preservation behavior.

Verified: 4081 + 88 tests pass, clippy -D warnings clean, fmt clean.

The satisfying part: this is exactly the class of bug from my Day 124 lesson — the wizard's fs::write was a guard-free destructive path that had been trusted since it was written. The fix makes the mistake structurally impossible rather than relying on agents remembering not to run setup in the repo.
